From: Alan de Bortolo <info@designmastersolutions.com>
Subject: [PATCH] print_task_config: keep the measured flow factor when the
 same filament is fed back after a runout

Fixes Snapmaker/u1-klipper#8 (runout + resume replaces the head's measured
flow factor with the class default, live and in flow_calibrator.json).

After a runout the RFID reader clears the head's filament info (no reset).
When the user feeds the spool back at the runout prompt, the reader's answer
reaches _rfid_filament_info_update_cb, which runs FLOW_RESET_K; for an
untagged spool the answer is the empty card, for a tagged one its tag. Then
Resume's INNER_CHECK_AND_RELOAD_FILAMENT_INFO restores the backed-up filament
("same filament, continue") and runs FLOW_RESET_K again. FLOW_RESET_K applies
the class default and saves it, so the factor measured by flow calibration is
lost for the rest of the print and for the next ones.

While paused, the reader's answer no longer resets the factor if the spool is
untagged or its tag names the backed-up vendor/type/sub-type; a tag for a
different filament still resets it, as before. INNER_CHECK_AND_RELOAD_FILAMENT_INFO
no longer resets it when it restores the backup. Outside a pause nothing changes.

diff --git a/klippy/extras/print_task_config.py b/klippy/extras/print_task_config.py
index ba2fe411..ec6bfdf5 100644
--- a/klippy/extras/print_task_config.py
+++ b/klippy/extras/print_task_config.py
@@ -366,10 +366,21 @@ class PrintTaskConfig:
             logging.error(f"[print_task_config] rfid info error: {str(e)}")
 
 
-        if is_clear == False:
+        if is_clear == False and not self._same_filament_reloaded(channel):
             # do not use run_script_from_command api
             self.gcode.run_script(f"FLOW_RESET_K EXTRUDER={channel}\r\n")
 
+    def _same_filament_reloaded(self, channel):
+        # A spool fed back while paused (the runout prompt) keeps the head's measured flow
+        # factor, unless its tag names another filament than the one backed up at the runout
+        pause_resume = self.printer.lookup_object('pause_resume', None)
+        if pause_resume is None or not pause_resume.is_paused:
+            return False
+        if self.print_task_config['filament_vendor'][channel] in ("", "NONE"):
+            return True
+        return all(self.print_task_config[key][channel] == self.filament_info_backup[key][channel]
+                   for key in ('filament_vendor', 'filament_type', 'filament_sub_type'))
+
     def reset_filament_info(self, extruder_index):
         if extruder_index < 0 or extruder_index >= PHYSICAL_EXTRUDER_NUM:
             logging.error(f"[print_task_config] reset_filament_info: extruder_index error: {extruder_index}")
@@ -883,7 +894,7 @@ class PrintTaskConfig:
                             self.print_task_config, DEFAULT_PRINT_TASK_CONFIG):
                         logging.error("[print_task_config] save print_task_config failed\r\n")
 
-                    self.gcode.run_script_from_command(f"FLOW_RESET_K EXTRUDER={extruder_index}\r\n")
+                    # same filament as before the runout: its measured flow factor stays
 
             except Exception as e:
                 logging.error("[print_task_config] INNER_CHECK_AND_RELOAD_FILAMENT_INFO error: %s", str(e))
